# Minimize exports

Export only what another module must call. Keep helpers, indexes, walkers, and intermediate types module-private. Extra exports couple callers to internals and freeze refactors.

```typescript
// ❌
export const indexTypeDoc = ...
export const mergeTypeDocs = ...
export const inheritOf = ...
export const getMappedTableName = ...

// ✅
const indexTypeDoc = ...
const typeIndex = ...
export const getMappedTableName = ...
```

Do not re-export a type that is only the function's parameter. Callers import `DatasourceData` (or the existing public type) instead of an alias invented for the helper. One export per concern; grow a barrel only when a second module needs the name.